{"id":"bs05","name":"Credit Limit Bands","lang":"sql","entry":null,"params":[],"limit_s":10,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>The risk team groups customers by credit limit. You have the table <b>customers</b> with the columns <code>customer_name</code> and <code>credit_limit</code> (numeric, never <code>NULL</code>, can have cents).</p>\n<p>The bands are:</p>\n<ul><li><code>'0-50k'</code>: from 0 to 50,000 included;</li><li><code>'50k-100k'</code>: more than 50,000 and up to 100,000 included;</li><li><code>'100k+'</code>: more than 100,000.</li></ul>\n<p>Your task is to return the columns <code>credit_band</code> and <code>customers</code> (the number of customers in the band), with the three bands always present (a band without customers has <code>0</code>), in the order of the list above.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>Table <code>customers</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>customer_name</th><th>credit_limit</th></tr><tr><td>Atelier</td><td>21000</td></tr><tr><td>Signal Gifts</td><td>71800</td></tr><tr><td>Aus Collectors</td><td>117300</td></tr><tr><td>La Rochelle</td><td>118200</td></tr><tr><td>Baane</td><td>81700</td></tr><tr><td>Mini Wheels</td><td>50000.5</td></tr></table></div><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>credit_band</th><th>customers</th></tr><tr><td>0-50k</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>50k-100k</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>100k+</td><td>2</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 10 seconds (psql)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB</div>","starter":"/* Write your PostgreSQL query here */\n","hints":["Écris les tranches avec < et >=, jamais BETWEEN 0 AND 50000 puis BETWEEN 50001 AND ... : 50000.50 tomberait dans le vide.","Pour afficher les tranches vides, pars d'une liste des 3 tranches (VALUES) et fais un LEFT JOIN."],"summary_fr":"Compter les clients par tranche de plafond de crédit, en affichant aussi les tranches vides (0), et sans trou entre les bornes (50000.50 doit tomber quelque part).","tags":["classes (bins)","CASE WHEN","bornes décimales","LEFT JOIN pour les classes vides"],"minutes":12,"source":"shawlu95/Beyond-LeetCode-SQL (MIT) · Group by Bins","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"tables":{"customers":{"columns":[["customer_name","VARCHAR(40)"],["credit_limit","NUMERIC(12,2)"]],"rows":[["Atelier",21000],["Signal Gifts",71800],["Aus Collectors",117300],["La Rochelle",118200],["Baane",81700],["Mini Wheels",50000.5]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["credit_band","customers"],"rows":[["0-50k",1],["50k-100k",3],["100k+",2]]}},{"input":{"tables":{"customers":{"columns":[["customer_name","VARCHAR(40)"],["credit_limit","NUMERIC(12,2)"]],"rows":[["A",0],["B",50000],["C",100000]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["credit_band","customers"],"rows":[["0-50k",2],["50k-100k",1],["100k+",0]]}}],"hidden_n":6,"hidden":"","solution":""}